      "round_summary": "Round 1/3: Fixed DUT bug in L5 state (line 243). Root cause: In L5, when contention cleared, the process returned to L4 without decrementing j(self). Since j(0)=1 from L3 and j(self)===self at L4 checks j(0)===0, process 0 could never enter L6 causing infinite L4↔L5 livelock (breaking pc0_entry_to_cs_progress, interested0_eventually_cleared, pc0_L4_j_eq_self_goes_L6, pc0_L4_j_neq_self_goes_L5, pc0_L5_progress_when_no_contention). Fix: added `j(self) := Mux(j(self) === 0.U, 0.U, j(self) - 1.U)` in the L5 no-contention branch so j(self) progressively decrements toward self. For process 0: j(0)=1→0 then j(0)===0→L6. All 5 failing assertions now reachable. Assertion labels preserved as-is; no homologous assertions (single L5 block).",
