      "round": 2,
      "round_summary": "Round 2/3: Fixed DUT bug in L6 state handler (line 255). Root cause: The L6 handler's `.otherwise` branch (exit critical section) only set `pc(self):=L7` without clearing `interested(self)`. The clearing was deferred to L7 handler (line 259), but `self` could change on the same cycle (via `io.select`), so L7 would clear a different process's interested flag instead. Causal path: L6 exit → interested(0) stays 1 → pc(0)=L7 but self already changed → L7 never fires for process 0 → interested(0) stuck at 1 → assertion fails. Fix: added `interested(self) := false.B` in L6 `.otherwise` branch before `pc(self) := Loc.L7`, ensuring the interested flag is cleared while `self` still points to the exiting process. Assertion labels preserved as-is. No homologous assertions (single L6 switch-case).",
